{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: terminal `null` outcomes after a desktop hop leave no user-visible feedback**

The in-flight half was fixed in the rework (30s waiting snack + the `_inFlight` latch — resolved thread), thank you. What remains silent is the **terminal** case: the core flows report cancel/timeout/malformed-callback exclusively through `onStatus` — e.g. `runCodeMieSsoCliFlow` returns `null` after "no SSO callback received (timeout or cancelled)", "CodeMie SSO callback carried no cookies", or "could not open browser automatically; open this URL manually: …" (`lib/src/cli/codemie_sso_server.dart`), and the same shape applies to the ChatGPT/AIIN flows (timeout, state mismatch, `FormatException`). In fa_ui every one of those lines lands in `_logStatus`, a `kDebugMode`-only `debugPrint`.

So on desktop, if the user abandons the browser step (or the browser never opened — the URL with the manual-fallback hint is debug-only too), the 30s "Waiting for the … sign-in" snack expires and a CodeMie wait can sit out its full 5-minute callback timeout with the picker looking frozen, then return `null` with **no terminal snack** — the only exception-path feedback is the `on Object` branch, which a `null` return never reaches.

Cheapest close-out (no stateful page needed): treat a desktop `null` after a real hop as a terminal outcome:

```dart
try {
  final result = await flow();
  if (result == null && context.mounted && _isDesktop) {
    showFahSnack(
      context,
      '$provider sign-in did not complete — cancelled or timed out.',
      hideCurrent: true,
    );
  }
  return result;
}
```

The full status-line-to-UI channel (live "waiting … (45s)" progress, manual-URL surfacing) stays a fair follow-up as agreed — this is only the "never end in silence" half, matching option C's own "explained, never silent" principle.

*(Non-blocking — the flows work end-to-end whenever the user completes the sign-in; failures reach the console log and the CLI behaves the same way in a terminal.)*
"}

